  "plan": "InstinctFlash plan for robbyant/lingbot-va-posttrain-robotwin\n  plan tier: NUMERIC\n  operating point: schedule {kv_refresh=2 + video=25 + action=50} | guidance {action=positive_only@1 [implied by mode], video=cfg@5 [inherited from the family default]} | cfg batching {batch-2 on 77 of 77 declared forwards (negative branch requested by video); batch-1 on 0}\n\n  skip   graph_capture              [BITEXACT  ] Thor capture performance is unmeasured for this family/operating point; retain the eager default pending a paired device measurement.\n  skip   engine_offload             [NUMERIC   ] precision='native': FP8 engine is not authorized; SM110: FP8 engine passes the declared dimension and denoise checks; action-horizon and observation/control compatibility still require validation\n  skip   pi05_tf32_numeric          [BITEXACT  ] checkpoint does not declare ['backbone:pi05', 'declares:pi05_tf32_numeric']; the pass is not applicable to it. This is a CAPABILITY decision, not a recipe one.\n  APPLY  fsdp_elision               [BITEXACT  ] world_size=1, so every FSDP all-gather is identity while still paying a flat-param copy and stream sync per unit per forward\n         expected: measured 1.75x standalone on LingBot-VA\n  APPLY  allocator_churn_elision    [BITEXACT  ] closed-loop serving has a stable working set, so releasing the pool between control steps only forces re-allocation next step\n         expected: small alone; larger once per-layer KV gathers stop churning the pool\n  APPLY  debug_dump_elision         [BITEXACT  ] per-chunk tensor dumps do a synchronous D2H on the critical path and are not consumed by the serving client\n         expected: measured ~1.10x on top of fsdp_elision\n  APPLY  obs_decode_elision         [BITEXACT  ] caller wants actions only; ['vae.decoder'] need never be resident or executed\n         expected: no latency win on this model (already skipped); frees resident memory, which is what sets episodes-per-GPU\n  APPLY  conditioning_prefill       [BITEXACT  ] ['text_kv', 'negative_text_kv'] declared pure in ['episode'] scope, but recomputed on all 77 forwards per control step (kv_refresh=2 + video=25 + action=50)\n         expected: hoists 2 artifact(s) out of the denoise loop. Measured ON LingBot-VA: 89 of 226 TFLOP per control cycle (39%), 67.6% of an action forward's layer FLOPs, 360 MiB resident. Those figures are that model's; for any other backbone the FLOP share and the residency cost follow its own layer count and artifact size. Launch-bound share means the wall-clock win is less than the FLOP win either way \u2014 measure it\n  skip   prompt_encoder_staging     [BITEXACT  ] no memory pressure on this device class (sm_110, 123 GiB): keeping the prompt encoder resident avoids per-reset PCIe moves and allocator churn\n  APPLY  ring_kv_addressing         [BITEXACT  ] streams ['video', 'action'] live across control steps in a pool that is currently addressed by boolean mask, costing a host sync and a full-pool copy per layer per forward\n         expected: measured 1.40x on LingBot-VA; measure this operating point and device (cost model: 223.3 ms)\n  APPLY  action_terminal_forward_elision [BITEXACT  ] the action phase's terminal forward writes provisional K/V that clear_pred_cache drops before any forward reads it; its output is discarded by construction\n         expected: one forward per cycle (the action pred-commit): 1 of 10 at 2V/4A, 1 of 8 at 2V/2A (cost model: 68.4 ms)\n  skip   sm120_gated_residual       [BITEXACT  ] hardware: needs sm_120, device is sm_110. This is a DEVICE decision, not a model one.\n  skip   sm120_wan_stage2           [BITEXACT  ] hardware: needs sm_120, device is sm_110. This is a DEVICE decision, not a model one.\n  APPLY  conv_layout_ndhwc          [NUMERIC   ] two Wan VAE Conv3D subgraphs can choose NCDHW or NDHWC by measurement on this device; NDHWC changes convolution accumulation order, so the swap is NUMERIC\n         expected: Measured ON H100: 1.405x complete cycle. RTX 5090 operator screen before integration: NCDHW 2.780 ms vs NDHWC 1.206 ms (2.30x); end-to-end must be measured and SM120 quality evidence is not inherited from H100.\n         decision: autotuned: va_conv_layout chose ndhwc over stock (1.76x), equivalence NUMERIC [measured]\n         decision: streaming_vae: 28 Conv3d weights -> ndhwc [NUMERIC] via cudnn_conv3d\n         decision: streaming_vae_half: 28 Conv3d weights -> ndhwc [NUMERIC] via cudnn_conv3d\n  skip   cfg_branch_elision         [NUMERIC   ] dropped by caller via Plan.without(): streams ['action'] discard their negative branch while ['video'] force batch duplication; forwards that can drop to batch 1 \u2014 action: 49 of 50 (commit steps exempt: their K/V feeds the other stream's negative branch)\n\n  NOTE: plan is NUMERIC because of ['conv_layout_ndhwc'].\n        Any accuracy-neutrality claim for this plan requires a paired\n        non-inferiority run.\n        `plan.bitexact_subset()` is the largest configuration that does not.",
